# CVE-2026-94545 — Next.js ImageResponse RCE

> **Severity:** 🔴 Critical — CVSS 9.5
> **Affected:** Next.js 16.2.0 – 16.3.5 (Node.js runtime, `sharp` installed)
> **Patched:** Next.js 16.3.6
> **Published:** September 24, 2026

## 📄 Full Report

👉 **[Read the full analysis (HTML)](./CVE-2026-94545-nextjs-imageresponse-rce.html)**

## ⚡ TL;DR

CVE-2026-94545 is a critical remote code execution vulnerability in the
Node.js implementation of `ImageResponse` from `next/og`. Attacker-controlled
values rendered into SVG content can escape Satori's sanitization and reach
native XML parsers via `sharp`, leading to memory corruption and RCE.

## 🎯 Affected Conditions (all must be true)

- Next.js `>=16.2.0 <16.3.6`
- Running on **Node.js runtime** (not Edge)
- `sharp` package installed
- Attacker-controlled input flows into generated SVG

## 🛡️ Remediation

```bash
npm install next@16.3.6
